  "section_notes": "The final text keeps the 5% test benchmark but removes any sales consequence: exceeding it triggers corrective action and regulator discretion only, which protects Northwind's Hearth 10 from an automatic ban. The 8-per-100k recall trigger is unchanged, but a recall is explicitly not a sales prohibition, which protects Halcyon's Ember 8 from a market ban. Per-model results go to customers but not the public, the retrofit window is 72 months (at the 6-year red-line edge), and built-in suppression starts at 36 months, as Halcyon required."
